# Python Rules

# Build System
- Use UV for dependency and virtual environments management
- Use pyproject.toml for project configuration
- Use Makefile for common tasks

# Testing Framework
- Use pytest for testing
- Use pytest-cov for coverage
- Use pytest-mock for mocking
- Maintain minimum 80% test coverage

# Code Style & Formatting
- Follow PEP 8 style guide
- Use Black for formatting
- Use isort for import sorting
- Use flake8 for linting
- Maximum line length is 88 characters (Black default)

# Project Structure
- Use src/ directory for source code
- Use tests/ directory for test files
- Follow Python package structure
- Use __init__.py files appropriately

# Dependencies & Libraries
- Use FastAPI for web applications
- Use SQLAlchemy for database access
- Use logging for proper logging
- Use python-dotenv for environment variables
- Use pydantic for data validation

# Security
- Never commit .env files
- Use proper input validation
- Follow OWASP security guidelines
- Use proper encryption
- Implement proper authentication

# Documentation
- Use Google style docstrings
- Keep README.md up to date
- Use Sphinx for documentation
- Include type hints
- Document all public APIs

# Performance
- Use proper async/await patterns
- Implement caching where appropriate
- Use proper error handling
- Follow Python performance best practices

# Version Control
- Use semantic versioning
- Write meaningful commit messages
- Use conventional commits
- Review code before merging

# Code Quality
- Run linting before commits
- Use mypy for type checking
- Regular code reviews required
- Use proper logging levels
- Implement proper error tracking
- Use pre-commit hooks 
